{"actor":{"type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# Product intent\n2\t\n3\t## Purpose\n4\t\n5\tTurnbridge lets a developer continue a visible coding conversation in a\n6\tdifferent agent CLI when they choose to switch providers or tools. It should\n7\tretain the full user-visible turn history—messages, tool calls, and tool\n8\tresults—rather than requiring a last-minute summary from a rate-limited model.\n9\t\n10\t## Behavioral commitments\n11\t\n12\t- Capture every available visible turn incrementally, not only on clean exit.\n13\t- Preserve source content faithfully and label its originating CLI.\n14\t- Offer one resume picker across supported CLIs while making the session type\n15\t  honest: native resume where possible, transcript rehydration otherwise.\n16\t- Prefer conversations whose repository and code state match the current work;\n17\t  warn rather than silently treating mismatched history as current.\n18\t- Never claim to transfer hidden reasoning, private provider state, or an\n19\t  exact native session.\n20\t- Put the developer in control of capture, sharing, and deletion.\n21\t\n22\t## Non-goals\n23\t\n24\t- A team presence system, task tracker, or agent orchestration framework.\n25\t- Inferring or replacing human intent.\n26\t- Depending on undocumented native session-file writes as its core mechanism.\n27\t\n28\t## Relationship to Conversation Ledger\n29\t\n30\tTurnbridge is a client of Conversation Ledger. It owns CLI-specific adapters\n31\tand rehydration behavior; Conversation Ledger owns the durable neutral record.\n32\t\n33\tExisting local transcript parsers should be reused where they are a good fit.\n34\tThey are adapters, not the canonical format: Turnbridge supplies the cursoring,\n35\tpartial-turn handling, and cross-CLI behavior those parsers do not promise.\n36\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01UvUovEDre47aa1CechSu88","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbri