{"actor":{"type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# WIP technical design\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** exploratory; adapter feasibility must be validated per CLI.\n4\t\n5\t## Main flow\n6\t\n7\t1. A source adapter discovers and tails the CLI's local transcript/session\n8\t   artifacts without modifying them.\n9\t2. After each completed visible turn, it normalizes newly observed material and\n10\t   appends it to Conversation Ledger.\n11\t3. A unified picker lists conversations compatible with the current repository,\n12\t   branch, `HEAD`, and user-selected sharing mode.\n13\t4. Native records for the selected CLI use its normal resume command. Imported\n14\t   records start a fresh target session and provide the complete canonical\n15\t   transcript as bootstrap context.\n16\t\n17\t## Adapter contract\n18\t\n19\tEach adapter must declare:\n20\t\n21\t- transcript discovery and incremental cursor semantics;\n22\t- how it identifies completed versus partial turns;\n23\t- role/content/tool-call normalization rules;\n24\t- repository/session identity extraction;\n25\t- known omissions and safe failure behavior.\n26\t\n27\tAdapters are readers first. Writing fabricated provider-native sessions may be\n28\texplored as an optional, version-pinned optimization but is not required for a\n29\tfunctional bridge and must never be the only recovery path.\n30\t\n31\tThe first Claude adapter should evaluate a pinned integration with an existing\n32\tlocal transcript extractor rather than reimplementing its format parser. The\n33\twrapper still owns an incremental cursor and must tolerate schema changes and\n34\tincomplete final lines.\n35\t\n36\t## Rehydration\n37\t\n38\tThe target adapter receives canonical events in order and constructs the\n39\tsmallest supported bootstrap mechanism: an initial prompt, a local transcript\n40\tfile plus an instruction to read it, or another documented import surface.\n41\tThe UI must say that the target is a new rehydrated session. It must preserve\n42\tliteral content, avoid silently summarizing, and report context-size limits\n43\tbefore launch.\n44\t\n45\t## CLI UX proposal\n46\t\n47\tAn executable shim may intercept familiar forms such as `claude --resume` and\n48\toffer a merged picker. Selecting a native Claude conversation delegates to\n49\tClaude. Selecting a Codex-origin conversation launches Claude through the\n50\trehydration path instead. Equivalent wrappers can serve other supported CLIs.\n51\t\n52\tDefault listings show only the current user's records that are compatible with\n53\tthe checked-out code. Future cross-user mode expands the list with clear author\n54\tand code-state labels.\n55\t\n56\t## Risks\n57\t\n58\tNative formats can change without notice; transcript content can include\n59\tsecrets; full histories consume substantial context; terminal processes can\n60\tcrash mid-turn. The MVP must retain raw incremental capture, present partial\n61\tcapture honestly, and provide redaction/local-only controls before any\n62\tautomatic sharing is enabled.\n63\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qq5bCs14us9nBM3S9nz2Md","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"db72655e67a3005a5585eb09e9faf6c5169bad5d","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","seq":18},"id":"ev1-9827359d18eb9240579b22a66b01ff2f6c2c00e65df8ac32b567c9a3bed9d84c","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-19T06:34:56.888Z","producer":{"session_id":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","source":"claude-code","tool":"cledger","version":"0.1.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"1\t# WIP technical design\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** exploratory; adapter feasibility must be validated per CLI.\n4\t\n5\t## Main flow\n6\t\n7\t1. A source adapter dis