{"actor":{"type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>adb79c2086870a6d6</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_0187nK8TS12MjfVvzLHLzizN</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-turnbridge/c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e/tasks/adb79c2086870a6d6.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Research git-ai and similar tools\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Research Report: Turnbridge Inspirations &amp; Prior Art\n\n### 1. \"git-ai\" — most likely **git-ai-project/git-ai** (github.com/git-ai-project/git-ai, originally acunniffe/git-ai)\n\n\"Git for the AI age.\" It's a git extension that attributes AI-written code at the line level. Coding agents call `git-ai checkpoint` as they write/edit code; on commit, git-ai stores line-level attribution (agent, model, session/prompt) in **Git Notes**, and preserves/re-maps that attribution through rebases, squashes, merges, resets, cherry-picks, and stashes. Attribution is self-reported by the agent (not heuristic detection), viewable via `git log --show-notes=\"ai\"`. Supports a wide agent roster: Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Codex, OpenCode, Windsurf, Droid, Amp, Gemini, Continue, and more, via an extensible integration framework. ~2.3k stars, 238 forks; claims adoption by \"hundreds of engineering teams including Fortune 100.\" Commercial cousin: usegitai.com. It does **not** address cross-CLI conversation resumption — its scope is attribution/provenance of code, not portable conversation state, and it stores metadata about commits, not full transcripts.\n\n### 2. The \"other popular public one\" — top candidates\n\n- **SpecStory** (specstory.com / github.com/specstoryai) — the strongest match. It wraps terminal agent invocations (`specstory run claude`, plus Cursor, Codex, Gemini, Droid CLI) and auto-saves every session — both sides of the chat plus `!`-command terminal output — as searchable Markdown at `.specstory/history/*.md` in your repo. Has a `specstory sync` command to convert/import prior native sessions after the fact. 100% local by default; cloud sync is opt-in. This is likely what the user means — it's the most visible \"auto-save your coding-agent sessions\" tool, spanning multiple CLIs, and ships as both a CLI wrapper and IDE extension.\n- **claude-code-log** (github.com/daaain/claude-code-log, ~1.2k stars) — converts Claude Code JSONL transcripts to readable HTML/Markdown. Notably has *experimental* provider support for other formats via `--provider agy|codex --session-id &lt;id&gt;` (Antigravity CLI, Codex CLI), i.e., it already has parsers for more than one native transcript schema — directly useful reference code for Turnbridge.\n- **claude-code-history-viewer** (github.com/jhlee0409/claude-code-history-viewer) — a desktop viewer claiming support for 28 AI coding assistants (Claude Code, Copilot, Gemini CLI, Codex CLI, Cursor Agent, etc.), letting you filter/compare across tools. Star count unlisted in search but worth checking directly.\n- Smaller single-purpose tools: `cchistory` (eckardt/cchistory, Claude Code bash-command history extractor) and `claude-history` (raine/claude-history, fuzzy search) — narrower scope, not cross-CLI.\n\n### 3. Directly relevant prior art for Turnbridge's core idea (capture → neutral ledger → resume in a different CLI)\n\nThis is worth flagging explicitly: several projects already attempt exactly Turnbridge's differentiator, not just adjacent transcript-viewing:\n- **cross_agent_session_resumer** (Dicklesworthstone/cross_agent_session_resumer) — converts Codex/Claude/Gemini native session formats through a **canonical intermediate representation**, then writes back into another tool's native format, with atomic writes/conflict handling. This is architecturally close to what Turnbridge is describing as its \"neutral ledger.\"\n- **cli-continues** (yigitkonur/cli-continues) — npx tool that auto-discovers and parses each tool's native session format (JSONL/JSON/SQLite/YAML), extracts messages/file-changes/tool-activity, and generates a handoff document injected into the target CLI.\n- **agent-session-resume** (hacktivist123/agent-session-resume) — a portable \"skill\" for continuing a session across Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Antigravity, OpenCode, Copilot without losing context/duplicating work.\n- **authsec-bridge** (blog: authsec.ai) — reads Claude Code/Codex/Gemini sessions off disk and rewrites them into the target CLI's exact session schema so the target's native `--resume` finds it as if it happened there.\n\n**File locations / formats (confirmed for parser-building):**\n- Claude Code: `~/.claude/projects/&lt;url-encoded-project-path&gt;/&lt;session-id&gt;.jsonl` — one JSONL file per session, escaped JSON with system prompts/metadata mixed in.\n- Codex CLI: `~/.codex/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/rollout-&lt;timestamp&gt;-&lt;uuid&gt;.jsonl` (override via `CODEX_HOME`); each rollout file has full conversation + tool calls + token usage.\n\n**Capture pattern differences:** git-ai does incremental *checkpoint* capture tied to git commits (metadata only, not full transcripts); SpecStory wraps the CLI process for live incremental capture *and* offers post-hoc sync/import; claude-code-log and the cross-agent resumer tools are purely post-hoc/on-demand parsers of the native JSONL files rather than incremental watchers. None of the sources found confirm a tool that does Turnbridge's full loop (incremental local capture → neutral ledger → resume in a *different* CLI) as a mature, widely-adopted product — the cross-agent resumers above are the closest but appear to be newer/smaller projects, suggesting real whitespace for Turnbridge.\n\nSources:\n- [git-ai (acunniffe/git-ai, now git-ai-project/git-ai)](https://github.com/acunniffe/git-ai)\n- [git-ai README](https://github.com/git-ai-project/git-ai/blob/main/README.md)\n- [Git AI product site](https://usegitai.com/)\n- [SpecStory Claude Code integration](https://docs.specstory.com/integrations/claude-code)\n- [SpecStory terminal coding agents overview](https://docs.specstory.com/integrations/terminal-coding-agents)\n- [SpecStory CLI](https://specstory.com/specstory-cli)\n- [claude-code-log](https://github.com/daaain/claude-code-log)\n- [claude-code-history-viewer](https://github.com/jhlee0409/claude-code-history-viewer)\n- [cchistory](https://github.com/eckardt/cchistory)\n- [claude-history](https://github.com/raine/claude-history)\n- [cross_agent_session_resumer](https://github.com/Dicklesworthstone/cross_agent_session_resumer)\n- [cli-continues](https://github.com/yigitkonur/cli-continues)\n- [agent-session-resume](https://github.com/hacktivist123/agent-session-resume)\n- [AuthSec bridge blog](https://authsec.ai/blogs/stop-re-explaining-bridge-claude-codex-gemini)\n- [Explore the .claude directory - Claude Code Docs](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/claude-directory)\n- [Codex CLI Config Location](https://inventivehq.com/knowledge-base/openai/where-configuration-files-are-stored)\n\nresult: Identified \"git-ai\" as git-ai-project/git-ai (line-level AI code attribution via git notes, ~2.3k stars, no cross-CLI resume) and the likely \"other popular tool\" as SpecStory (auto-saves Claude Code/Codex/Gemini/Cursor sessions to Markdown); also surfaced closer direct competitors to Turnbridge itself (cross_agent_session_resumer, cli-continues, agent-session-resume) plus confirmed file paths (`~/.claude/projects/*.jsonl`, `~/.codex/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/rollout-*.jsonl`) and an existing open-source JSONL parser (claude-code-log) for reference.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>30412</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>9</tool_uses><duration_ms>67267</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","type":"text"}],"role":"user"},"conte