oss-CLI resume) and the likely \"other popular tool\" as SpecStory (auto-saves Claude Code/Codex/Gemini/Cursor sessions to Markdown); also surfaced closer direct competitors to Turnbridge itself (cross_agent_session_resumer, cli-continues, agent-session-resume) plus confirmed file paths (`~/.claude/projects/*.jsonl`, `~/.codex/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/rollout-*.jsonl`) and an existing open-source JSONL parser (claude-code-log) for reference.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>30412</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>9</tool_uses><duration_ms>67267</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","role":"user"},"origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"parentUuid":"2958eb60-6cff-434b-982f-a2ebe60de627","permissionMode":"auto","promptId":"1aa45a5c-10bc-4de1-b568-04646f4cf2cc","promptSource":"system","sessionId":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","slug":"generic-stirring-candy","timestamp":"2026-07-19T06:36:45.080Z","type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"74dafcc9-3dca-46e0-b27f-0c4b20cb1ae6","version":"2.1.215"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-07-19T06:36:49.565Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
{"actor":{"type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ae919d75da37c7146</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01AyiufciuuCR6Qb9avLvcHR</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-turnbridge/c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e/tasks/ae919d75da37c7146.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Explore conversation-ledger dependency\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Confirmed: `package.json` has no `main`/`exports`/`types` field — only `bin`. This is a report-only exploration task, so I'll now summarize findings.\n\n## Conversation Ledger — exploration report\n\n**Repo:** `/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger` (v0.1.0, single commit `1f7b031`)\n\n### 1. Implementation state\nReal, working TypeScript, not design-only. `src/` has full implementation + `src/test/*.test.ts`; `dist/` has compiled JS matching `src/` 1:1 (built via `tsc`). `npm test` runs `node --test dist/test/**/*.test.js`. However, **`package.json` has no `\"main\"`/`\"exports\"`/`\"types\"` field** — only `\"bin\": {\"conversation-ledger\": \"dist/cli.js\", \"cledger\": \"dist/cli.js\"}`. So today the *only* supported public surface is the `cledger` CLI (plus piping JSON to `cledger append`/reading `cledger export` JSON). There is no published importable module entry point for Turnbridge to `import` from directly, even though the internal TS functions are clean and exported from their files (`src/store.ts`, `src/schema.ts`, `src/git.ts`).\n\n### 2. Public API surface\nCLI commands (`src/cli.ts`): `append` (stdin JSONL of `EventDraft`s), `log`, `show &lt;conv-id-prefix&gt;`, `conversations`, `export`, `sync`, `install &lt;claude-code|codex|all&gt;`, `hook &lt;claude-code|codex&gt;` (stdin: hook payload), `capture &lt;claude-code|codex&gt; --transcript PATH`.\n\nUnderlying TS functions (not exported as a package, but these are the real API shapes a Node consumer would use if importing from `dist/` directly):\n- `appendEvents(repo: RepoInfo, drafts: EventDraft[], opts?: {context?: RepoContext}): Promise&lt;AppendResult&gt;` — `src/store.ts:134`. `AppendResult = { appended: EvidenceEvent[]; deduped: number; anchor: string | null }`.\n- `readEvents(repo: RepoInfo, opts?: ReadOptions): Promise&lt;EvidenceEvent[]&gt;` — `src/store.ts:209`. `ReadOptions = { reachableFrom?, kind?, source?, conversation? }`.\n- `sortEvents(events)`, `sync(repo, remote?, mode?: \"both\"|\"push\"|\"fetch\")`, `listAnchors`, `readNoteEvents`, `captureContext(repo): Promise&lt;RepoContext&gt;`.\n- Schema helpers (`src/schema.ts`): `finalizeEvent(draft, now?)`, `eventId(draft)`, `validateEvent(event)`, `serializeEvent`, `parseEventLine`.\n- `findRepo(dir): Promise&lt;RepoInfo|null&gt;` (`src/git.ts`) — resolves `{root, gitDir}`.\n- Adapters: `captureClaudeTranscript(transcriptPath, cwd)` and `runClaudeCodeHook(stdinJson)` in `src/adapters/claude-code.ts`; equivalents for Codex in `src/adapters/codex.ts`.\n\n### 3. Canonical data model\n`EvidenceEvent` (`src/schema.ts`): `id` (`\"ev1-\" + sha256` of an identity subset), `schema` (`\"conversation-ledger/v1\"`), `kind` (open string; well-known: `conversation_turn, decision, document, annotation, redaction, supersession`), `occurred_at`/`recorded_at` (ISO8601), `actor: {type, id?, display?}` (human/agent/system), `producer: {tool, version?, source?, session_id?}`, `media_type?`, `content: unknown`, `context?: {repo, branch, head, cwd, dirty_fingerprint}`, `conversation?: {id, seq}` (id like `claude-code:&lt;session-uuid&gt;`, seq = source line index), `links?: [{rel, target}]`, `raw?: {format, data}` (opaque source-native payload, e.g. `claude-code-jsonl/1`, `codex-rollout-jsonl/1`).\n\nConversation turns: `content = { role, blocks }` where blocks pass through text/tool_use/tool_result verbatim; `thinking` blocks kept minus opaque signature; Codex's encrypted reasoning is dropped, never stored.\n\nStorage: one git note per anchor commit under `refs/notes/conversation-ledger`; note body = JSONL, canonical-JSON (sorted keys, `src/canonical.ts`) per line, sorted+unique. Events anchor to `HEAD` at capture time, so they ride the commit DAG. Merge strategy `cat_sort_uniq` configured per-ref. No content lives outside the note blob (GC-safe, no external pointers).\n\n### 4. Cursoring / idempotency / append semantics\n- **Idempotency**: `eventId()` hashes only the durable/source-determined subset (`schema, kind, occurred_at, actor.type/id, producer.source/session_id, conversation, media_type, content, links`) — excludes `recorded_at, context, raw, producer.tool/version`. Re-scanning always yields the same id.\n- **Append** (`appendEvents`): reads existing note lines for the current HEAD anchor, dedupes by `id` against a `Set`, merges in any queued \"pending\" events, writes back sorted+unique lines via `git notes add -f -F -`. File-lock (`.git/conversation-ledger/lock`) guards concurrent writers, with a 10s steal timeout.\n- **Unborn HEAD**: events queue to `.git/conversation-ledger/pending.jsonl` and flush into the first real commit's note.\n- **Per-adapter cursor**: `.git/conversation-ledger/cursors/&lt;sessionId&gt;.json` stores `{lines: number}` — line-count offset into the source transcript, purely a perf optimization (resets to 0 if transcript is shorter than expected); correctness relies on `eventId` dedup, not the cursor.\n- **Reading**: `readEvents` supports `reachableFrom` (branch-scoped via `git rev-list`), `kind`, `source`, `conversation` (prefix match) filters; `sortEvents` orders by conversation id, then `seq`, then `occurred_at`, then `id`.\n- **Sync**: fully separate, explicit-only (`cledger sync`) — never runs implicitly during append/capture.\n\n### 5. Docs on intended clients/division of responsibilities\n`docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md` and README explicitly define a 3-tier ecosystem: **conversation-ledger** (neutral storage: normalized, provenance-preserving evidence, never summarizes/ranks/interprets) → **turnbridge** (records/transfers visible conversations between coding CLIs) → **intent-recall** (later retrieves evidence to reason about original/superseded intent). Non-goals explicitly punted to Turnbridge/Intent Recall: deciding which historical statement is correct, summarizing/embedding, controlling/orchestrating agents. `docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md` header: \"Status: implemented in v0.1; format may still evolve until v1.\"\n\n### 6. Gaps for a client like Turnbridge\n- **No importable library surface** — no `main`/`exports`/`types` in `package.json`; Turnbridge would have to shell out to the `cledger` binary or reach into `dist/*.js` unofficially.\n- No Turnbridge-specific adapter yet — only `claude-code` and `codex` adapters exist; if Turnbridge normalizes turns itself (per its own description) it would call `cledger append` with pre-built `EventDraft` JSON (documented: `echo '{\"kind\":\"decision\",...}' | cledger append`), but there's no adapter/import path tailored to \"already-normalized turns from an external tool.\"\n- No secret redaction at capture (roadmap item, tool output stored verbatim — high risk for a capture pipeline).\n- No squash-merge re-anchoring (conversations can drop out of branch reachability after squash-merge).\n- No sub-turn citation anchors (explicitly future work for intent-recall).\n- No format-drift detection/warning when adapters silently skip unrecognized transcript line types.\n- No purge/true-deletion tooling, only append-only `redaction` events.\n- No `Conversation` manifest object — conversation identity is implicit via `conversation.id`/`seq` fields only.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>36291</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>11</tool_uses><duration_ms>54030</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","type":"t